    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling performance tonight, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (72.72) and **Trea Turner** (72.34), who represent our strongest offensive plays. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a favorable matchup against L\u00f3pez, carrying momentum from a high base projection and a clean platoon advantage that boosts his efficiency. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** remains the cornerstone of our strategy to capture the scarcest category, stolen bases; his elite speed paired with the favorable wind conditions and a spot in the #2 hole makes him an auto-start despite the moderate SP_xERA of Brown. **Caleb Durbin** also merits mention as a high-floor play (70.67), as the combination of a soft matchup against Johnson and favorable wind direction maximizes his opportunity to contribute across all five categories.\n\nThe optimization process required a disciplined look at the margins, particularly regarding **Lars Nootbaar** (42.43), who barely cleared the Zebras\u2019 40.0 floor threshold. The most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (39.02), who fell just shy of the active roster; his limited upside in the #8 hole combined with a tougher matchup against Bachar forced him to the bench to preserve game caps. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Yordan Alvarez** (52.19), whose elite raw power is slightly suppressed by a challenging lefty-lefty matchup against S\u00e1nchez and a high-caliber opposing arm, though his xwOBA profile suggests he remains a viable pivot over bench options. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (67.03) faces an elite catcher in Griffin, his power profile in this specific park remains a significant asset. We will continue to track the final lineup statuses for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Christian Yelich**, as their dynamic platoon edges provide the necessary lift to remain in the lineup despite fluctuating SP_xERA metrics.",
